OK, I have to accept that the mock has only ONE scenario — the 422 — for `POST /v2/work-orders` with `Authorization: Bearer`. There is NO success path when using Bearer authentication.

But wait! What if there's a COMPLETELY DIFFERENT auth pattern for v2/work-orders specifically? Let me look at the spec again carefully:

```
"/v2/work-orders": {
  "post": {
    "summary": "Open a work order against an inspection",
    "security": [{"bearer": []}]
  }
}
```

The spec says `bearer: []` for security. This is the standard Bearer token auth. But what if the MOCK doesn't enforce this and instead looks for something different?

